# Vercel must not see this as a Python application.
#
# PCIS is a STATIC site: the Python runs in the visitor's browser via
# Pyodide/WebAssembly, and Vercel only ever serves files. But Vercel's
# framework detection sees pyproject.toml at the repo root, concludes
# this is a Python serverless app, and fails with:
#
#   "No python entrypoint found. Set tool.vercel.entrypoint ..."
#
# Excluding the Python project from the deployment upload removes that
# signal entirely. It also makes deploys faster, since only web/ is
# transferred -- the desktop app, tests and build tooling are
# irrelevant to serving a static page.
#
# NOTE: web/pcis_core.zip is NOT excluded. It is the engineering core
# the browser loads, and the site is broken without it.

pyproject.toml
requirements.txt
pcis/
tests/
tools/
assets/
docs/
*.spec
*.bat
*.ps1
*.md
LICENSE
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
installer_output/
Release/
*.db
*.egg-info
installer.iss
sample_report.pdf
.gitignore
